cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "MEMOIR: Memory Evaluation over Multi-year Oncology Inference & Retrieval"
message: "If you use this benchmark, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
authors:
  - name: "Olira"
    website: "https://olira.ai"
abstract: >-
  A benchmark for the memory substrate underneath a clinical agent. 117 synthetic
  oncology patients with complete multi-year records and 3,617 questions across
  four tasks (point-in-time lookup, needle-in-the-record event detection,
  clinical episode synthesis, and time-series and trajectory reasoning) with the
  scorers that grade them and an agent harness that holds everything above the
  memory layer constant, so the substrate is the only variable.
keywords:
  - benchmark
  - clinical AI
  - agent memory
  - longitudinal health records
  - temporal reasoning
  - evaluation
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/olira-ai/memoir-benchmark"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-09-11"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22906151"
references:
  - type: data
    title: "mCODE Test Data"
    authors:
      - name: "HL7 CodeX"
    year: 2023
    url: "https://confluence.hl7.org/spaces/COD/pages/80119851/mCODE+Test+Data"
    notes: "Source synthetic oncology records the corpus is derived from."
  - type: article
    title: "Synthea: An approach, method, and software mechanism for generating synthetic patients and the synthetic electronic health care record"
    authors:
      - family-names: "Walonoski"
        given-names: "Jason"
    year: 2018
    doi: "10.1093/jamia/ocx079"
